WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.112
A condition is simply a question that Python can answer with True or False.

00:00:05.112 --> 00:00:10.372
Sales greater than target asks whether one number is larger than another.

00:00:10.372 --> 00:00:15.562
Status equal to Open asks whether two values match exactly.

00:00:15.562 --> 00:00:20.474
Returns not equal to zero asks whether a value is different from zero.

00:00:21.056 --> 00:00:27.188
The comparison operators in the table are worth recognizing: double equals compares equality,

00:00:27.188 --> 00:00:34.523
exclamation equals means not equal, and the greater-than and less-than symbols can also include equality.

00:00:34.523 --> 00:00:38.493
These comparisons become the decision points in if statements.
